AttributeType [SimTalk] - FlowControl
Sets the data type of the attribute that determines how the FlowControl designated by <Path> moves the
MUs on.
Remarks
AttributeType applies to the Exit Strategy > MU Attribute.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.AttributeType:string
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type string.
Example
MyFlowControl.AttributeType := "integer"
See also
MU Attribute [FlowControl, exit]
AttributeType [SimTalk] - FlowControl
11-2612 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

DefaultSuccessor [SimTalk] - FlowControl
Sets the number of the default successor to which the FlowControl designated by <Path> moves the MUs.
Remarks
DefaultSuccessor applies if none of the MUs has an attribute with the Value you entered into the
DataTable. To not move a MU, which does not meet one of the conditions on the table, specify 0.
To show a message, when a MU is to be moved which does not meet any of the conditions in the
DataTable, specify -1.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.DefaultSuccessor:integer
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type integer.
Example
MyFlowControl.DefaultSuccessor := 1
See also
MU Attribute [FlowControl, exit]
MU Name
DefaultSuccessor [SimTalk] - FlowControl
Plant Simulation Help 11-2613
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

EntryBehavior [SimTalk]
Sets the strategy according to which the FlowControl designated by <Path> receives the MUs from its
predecessors.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.EntryBehavior:string
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type string.
• To cyclically receive the MUs from all predecessors, specify Cyclic.
• To cyclically receive the MUs from the predecessor according to the sequence of predecessors, which
you typed into the list, specify Cyclic Sequence.
• To receive the MUs from the predecessor in the order in which they intended to exit, specify First come,
first served.
• To receive the MUs from the predecessor that has not provided a MU for the longest time, specify Least
recently used.
• To receive the MUs from the predecessor defined by the return value of a Method, specify Method.
• To receive the MUs from the predecessor, from which the FlowControl received a MU the last time,
specify Most recently used.
• To receive the MUs from the predecessors according to a percentage distribution, specify Percentage.
• To receive the MUs from the predecessors in a random fashion, specify Random.
• To receive the MUs from the predecessors according to the state and the material flow balance of the
predecessors, specify Selection. Then, specify a Property.
• To receive the MUs from the first available predecessor, specify Start at Predecessor 1.
Example
MyFlowControl.EntryBehavior := "random"
See also
Strategy [FlowControl, entry]
EntryBehavior [SimTalk]
11-2614 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

