EntrySelectionMethod [SimTalk]
Sets the name of the Method object, which the FlowControl designated by <Path> uses.
Remarks
EntrySelectionMethod applies when you set the attribute EntryBehavior to Method.
Note
You cannot move or delete MUs in the Method because Plant Simulation calls the Method like a formula.
For this reason Plant Simulation does not show the tab Expressions of the Method Debugger.
In addition, you cannot use a wait-instruction, a waituntil-instruction, or a stopuntil-instruction
within the Method.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.EntrySelectionMethod:method
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type method.
Example
MyFlowControl.EntryBehavior := "method"
MyFlowControl.EntrySelectionMethod := &myMethod
See also
EntryBehavior [SimTalk]
Method [FlowControl, entry]
Tab Expressions [Watch window]
