ExitBehavior [SimTalk]
Sets the strategy according to which the FlowControl designated by <Path> moves the MUs on its
successors.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.ExitBehavior:string
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type string.
• The strategy Assignment does not determine the successor to which the FlowControl moves the MU.
Instead, you can change the values of the attributes of the MU, when it moves to the one and only
successor of the FlowControl. As soon as the MU is moved on to the successor, Plant Simulation calls the
Method, whose name you entered into the text box Method. Define the assignments to be made in this
Method.
• To move the MUs cyclically on to all successors, specify Cyclic.
• To cyclically move the MUs on to the successor according to the sequence of successors, which you
typed into a list, specify Cyclic Sequence.
• To move the MUs on to the successor, which has been Waiting the longest for a MU, specify Least
recently used.
• To move the MUs on to a successor according to the return value of a Method, specify Method.
Note
You cannot move or delete MUs in the Method because Plant Simulation calls the Method like
a formula. For this reason Plant Simulation does not show the tab Expressions of the Method
Debugger.
In addition, you cannot use a wait-instruction, a waituntil-instruction, and a stopuntil-instruction
within the Method.
• To move the MUs on to the successor, which has Waiting the shortest time for a MU, specify Most
recently used.
• To move the MUs on to a successor according to the values of attributes of the MUs, specify MU
Attribute.
• To move the MUs on to a successor according to their names, specify MU Name.
• To move the MUs on to a successor according to a percentage distribution, specify Percentage.
ExitBehavior [SimTalk]
Plant Simulation Help 11-2619
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

• To move the MUs on to a randomly selected successor, specify Random.
• To move the MUs on to the successor meeting a certain Property, specify Selection. Then, specify a
Property.
• To move the MUs on to the first available successor, specify Start at Successor 1.
• To copy the MUs that enter, and move a copy each to each of the successors, specify To all Successors.
Example
MyFlowControl.ExitBehavior := "random"
See also
Strategy [FlowControl, exit]
ExitBehavior [SimTalk]
11-2620 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

